            "For a 420 sq. ft. exterior wall area with 10-inch walls, you will need roughly 10 to 12 cubic meters of material, and since you prioritize speed over hand-mixing, pre-cast blocks are definitely your best route. They arrive fully cured and ready to stack, which bypasses the wet-casting and drying wait times entirely. Keep in mind that your timber or steel frame carries the actual roof and floor loads, while the hempcrete acts as your continuous, highly insulating infill. These planning estimates are great for budgeting, though you'll still want a local engineer or designer to review final details for permitting under the 2024 IRC Appendix BL. \n\nWould you prefer to explore using 12-inch walls for maximum thermal performance, or stick with the 10-inch thickness to maximize your interior floor space?"
